[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
Below is a concise “check-list → code → notes” for the two plugins you mentioned.  
It assumes you have already completed the **core migration steps** (swap the package, change `mapboxgl` → `maplibregl`, drop the Mapbox access token, and point the map at a non-Mapbox style). If you haven’t, do those first – otherwise the plugins will still try to talk to Mapbox services and you’ll see 401/404 errors.

---

## 1️⃣ `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw`

### What you can keep
* The **JavaScript library** itself works unchanged – it only uses the Mapbox GL JS public API (`addControl`, `addSource`, `addLayer`, `on`, …) which MapLibre still provides.
* All drawing logic (polygon, line, point, edit, delete, etc.) stays the same.

### What you must change

| Item | Old (Mapbox) | New (MapLibre) | How to change |
|------|--------------|----------------|---------------|
| **Import** | `import MapboxDraw from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw';` | Same import (the package name does not change) | No code change. |
| **CSS class prefix** | Styles reference `.mapboxgl-ctrl-draw-*` and `.mapboxgl-draw-*` | MapLibre’s CSS prefix is `.maplibregl-` | 1. **Replace the CSS file** you load from the draw package (it ships a `mapbox-gl-draw.css`). 2. Add a tiny override that rewrites the class names, or copy the CSS and rename the selectors. Example:  <br>```css\n/* mapbox-gl-draw.css → maplibre-gl-draw.css */\n.mapboxgl-ctrl-draw-btn { … } → .maplibregl-ctrl-draw-btn { … }\n.mapboxgl-draw-point { … } → .maplibregl-draw-point { … }\n```<br>Or, if you prefer not to edit the CSS, just add a global rule that maps the old names to the new ones: <br>```css\n.mapboxgl-ctrl-draw-btn, .mapboxgl-draw-point { all: unset; }\n.maplibregl-ctrl-draw-btn, .maplibregl-draw-point { /* original styles */ }\n``` |
| **Control addition** | `map.addControl(new MapboxDraw());` | Same call, but the control’s CSS class now starts with `maplibregl-` | No JavaScript change needed. |
| **Optional – use a MapLibre-native fork** | N/A | `terra-draw` (actively maintained for MapLibre) | If you want to avoid the CSS rename, install the fork: <br>```bash\nnpm i terra-draw terra-draw-maplibre-gl-adapter\n```<br>Then: <br>```javascript\nimport { TerraDrawMapLibreGLAdapter } from 'terra-draw-maplibre-gl-adapter';\nimport { TerraDrawPolygonMode } from 'terra-draw';\n\nconst draw = new TerraDraw({\n  adapter: new TerraDrawMapLibreGLAdapter({ map: map }),\n  modes: [new TerraDrawPolygonMode()],\n});\n```<br>Both approaches work; pick the one you prefer. |

### Quick “copy-paste” example (keep the original draw package)

```html
<!-- index.html -->
<link href="node_modules/@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw/dist/mapbox-gl-draw.css" rel="stylesheet">
```

```css
/* maplibre-draw.css – place after the original CSS so it overrides */
.mapboxgl-ctrl-draw-btn { /* old selector */ }
.maplibregl-ctrl-draw-btn { /* copy the rules from the line above */ }

.mapboxgl-draw-point { /* old selector */ }
.maplibregl-draw-point { /* copy the rules */ }

/* repeat for .mapboxgl-draw-line, .mapboxgl-draw-polygon, etc. */
```

```javascript
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import MapboxDraw from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw/dist/mapbox-gl-draw.css';
import './maplibre-draw.css';   // ← our overrides

const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

const draw = new MapboxDraw({
  displayControlsDefault: false,
  controls: {
    polygon: true,
    line_string: true,
    point: true,
    trash: true
  }
});

map.addControl(draw);
```

> **Tip:** If you ever upgrade to MapLibre v6+, the CSS class prefix change is still the only thing you need to keep in mind – the JavaScript API is stable.

